# A worker that works for the app on another machine (the Pi): copy to worker/.env, fill in, run `make remote-worker`.
# Reachability: Tailscale on every machine is easiest (the same names work at home and away).

# The name shown in the app (Instellingen). Unique per machine.
WORKER_NAME=pc-4080
# How the app on the Pi reaches this machine, on port 8001: its Tailscale name, or its Tailscale IP
# (`tailscale ip -4`, always works from inside the Pi's containers).
WORKER_PUBLIC_URL=http://pc-4080:8001
# How this machine reaches the app: the same address as APP_URL in the .env on the Pi.
WORKER_APP_URL=https://creatorsmp4.example.nl
# The same WORKER_TOKEN as in the .env on the Pi.
WORKER_TOKEN=

# Optional:
# Which tasks this machine takes: transcribe,extract (default) or one of them.
#WORKER_CAPABILITIES=transcribe,extract
# The free worker with the highest priority goes first. Default: cuda 100, mlx 50, cpu 10.
#WORKER_PRIORITY=100
# 2 on a 16 GB GPU (RTX 4080): Whisper and Qwen stay loaded together. 1 on an 8 GB GPU.
#WORKER_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=2
# Needed on a Mac, so the app can reach the native worker (Docker workers listen on all interfaces anyway).
#WORKER_HOST=0.0.0.0
# Model settings: the defaults are in worker/cuda.env (Docker) and scripts/worker-mac.sh (Mac).
